// Expected: c0 at one session and at two.
//
// Replication must not manufacture cryptographic material. The secret is
// long-term, so both sessions split the *same* value, and share_a#2 is the
// same term as share_a rather than a second, independent share. One share
// reaches the wire per session; two sessions of one share are still one
// share, and SHAMIR_JOIN needs two distinct ones.
//
// This is the model to look at if session expansion ever starts freshening
// something it should share, or if the attacker's knowledge set stops
// deduplicating by equivalence: either mistake would hand the attacker a
// second share it never received and reconstruct a secret that is safe.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private secret_s
	share_a, share_b, share_c = SHAMIR_SPLIT(secret_s)
]

Alice -> Bob: share_a

principal Bob[
	digest_b = HASH(share_a)
]

queries[
	confidentiality? secret_s
]
